    "deprecated": false,
    "description": "Read operation. Retrieve all required pages before reporting complete totals. Returns a paginated list of the account's payment methods. This is a v2 native-entity endpoint served from the `/v2/api/entity` base and authenticated with a Bearer token.\n\nThe trailing path segment (`1`) is the **data level** — how deeply related records are loaded — not a page number. On this endpoint the data level has no visible effect, so `/site_payment_gateway/list` and `/site_payment_gateway/list/1` return the same result. Pagination is controlled by the `page` and `per_page` query parameters.\n\n| Parameter | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `page` | Page number (default `1`). |\n| `per_page` | Items per page (default `20`). |\n| `filter[<field>]` | Filter by an exact field value, e.g. `filter[active]=1` returns only active methods. |\n\nThe response is a standard paginated envelope. Each item in `data` is a payment-method record that also embeds its related `treasury` and `branch` objects.",
